      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa_Arizona_Temple",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rail service arrived in Mesa in December 1895 when the Maricopa & Phoenix & Salt River Valley Railroad began running trains to Tempe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mesaaz.gov/Government/About-Mesa/Mesa-History",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The University of Arizona opened a research station on Main Street in 1914, testing new crops for local farmers until its closure in 1983.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mesaaz.gov/Government/About-Mesa/Mesa-History",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Mesa Canal, built by early colonists, transformed an abandoned Hohokam canal into the town’s primary irrigation artery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
